{
  "slug": "as-of-july-2026-financial-and-bankruptcy-status-of-6c2b2dbf",
  "query": "As of July 2026, financial and bankruptcy status of these companies: Chegg Inc, America's Car-Mart Inc, JetBlue Airways, Peloton Inc, Faraday Future Intelligent Electric, Petco Health and Wellness. Which are at highest risk of bankruptcy filing in mid-2026? Any going concern warnings, debt maturities, or restructuring news?",
  "answer": "Research complete. Here's the summary of my findings on the six companies' bankruptcy risk as of July 2026:\n\n## Highest Bankruptcy Risk (mid-2026)\n\n1. **Faraday Future (FFAI, formerly FFIE)** — The clearest candidate. Explicit going-concern warning in Q1 2026 10-Q; only **$12.2M cash**, negative working capital ~$76M, $4.7B accumulated deficit, $512K quarterly revenue, $42.3M loss. Stock at ~$0.11, down ~97%. Surviving on dilutive convertible notes.\n\n2. **America's Car-Mart (CRMT)** — Explicit going-concern warning in its FY2026 annual report (July 14, 2026), citing risk of \"restructuring, bankruptcy or liquidation.\" $722M debt, no revolver, FY diluted EPS of **-$16.79**, closed 60 of 154 dealerships.\n\n## Moderate-Elevated (multi-year, not acute mid-2026)\n\n3. **JetBlue (JBLU)** — No formal going-concern warning, but analysts flag ~75% bankruptcy odds by 2027 (CCC+ territory). Over $5B debt, $319M Q1 loss, $1.77B balloon due 2029 — but cushioned by ~$2.4B liquidity, $3B capex deferral, and new $500M financing.\n\n## Low Risk\n\n4. **Chegg (CHGG)** — Only $33.9M of notes due Sept 2026 vs. $67.9M cash; solvent but revenue collapsing (-48% YoY) on AI disruption; stock sub-$1.\n5. **Petco (WOOF)** — Refinanced, maturities pushed to 2031, ~$654M liquidity, EBITDA guidance raised. Turnaround.\n6. **Peloton (PTON)** — Lowest risk: ~$1.13B cash, 1.1x leverage, positive Q3 net income, expects first-ever full-year profit in FY2026.\n\n**Bottom line:** Faraday Future and America's Car-Mart are the two with active going-concern warnings and genuine mid-2026 bankruptcy exposure. Full sourced data has been delivered via the structured output.\n\nNote: AskNews news search was unavailable (inactive subscription), so news findings rely on web search of SEC filings, earnings releases, and financial media.",
